+    Pass ``reverse=True`` to sort the groups in descending order
+    instead of ascending, for example to list the most recent or the
+    highest values first.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        <ul>{% for age, items in users|groupby("age", reverse=true) %}
+          <li>{{ age }}: {{ items|map(attribute="name")|join(", ") }}</li>
+        {% endfor %}</ul>
+
+    You can pass a callable as ``key_transform`` to change how each
+    group key is displayed, for example to format a date. The items are
+    still sorted and grouped by the original attribute value, only the
+    ``grouper`` that is yielded is the result of calling the function
+    with that value.
+
+    .. sourcecode:: jinja
+
+        {% for month, items in posts|groupby("date", key_transform=format_month) %}
+          <h2>{{ month }}</h2>
+        {% endfor %}
+
+    .. versionchanged:: 3.1
+        Added the ``key_transform`` parameter.
+
+    .. versionchanged:: 3.1
+        Added the ``reverse`` parameter.
+
     .. versionchanged:: 3.0
         Added the ``default`` parameter.
 
